# Tests for meshes & CGO helpers

After changes here, run:

```bash
pytest tests/unit/test_rebuild.py tests/unit/test_cgo_tokens.py tests/unit/test_line_style.py -q
```

- `util/cgo.py` `resolve_cgo_tokens` — numeric strings like `'0.86'` must stay floats, not opcodes (`test_cgo_tokens.py`)
- `util/line_style.py` — dash segment counts, margins (`test_line_style.py`)
- `Sphere`, `Cylinder`, `Arrows`, etc. — construct with literal xyz, `rebuild(None)`, token-shape snapshots in `test_rebuild.py`

Do not compare full float vertex dumps; check opcode kinds and counts.
